<quiz>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_CHEMISTRY_BIOMOLECULES_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Identifying the anomeric carbon of glucopyranose</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The Haworth representation of \(\alpha\)-D-(+)-glucopyranose is shown below:</p>
<div style="text-align:center; margin:10px 0;">
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 340 220" width="340" height="220" style="background:#ffffff; font-family:sans-serif;">
  <polygon points="100,80 170,50 240,80 240,140 170,170 100,140" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  <circle cx="205" cy="65" r="14" fill="#ffffff"/>
  <text x="200" y="71" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" fill="#000000">O</text>
  <!-- C1 -->
  <line x1="240" y1="140" x2="275" y2="155" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="280" y="160" font-size="14" fill="#800080" font-weight="bold">OH</text>
  <line x1="240" y1="140" x2="240" y2="105" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="236" y="100" font-size="14" fill="#000000">H</text>
  <text x="250" y="135" font-size="14" fill="#d9534f" font-weight="bold">C1</text>
  <!-- C2 -->
  <line x1="170" y1="170" x2="170" y2="205" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="160" y="218" font-size="14" fill="#800080" font-weight="bold">OH</text>
  <text x="165" y="160" font-size="14" fill="#000000">H</text>
  <text x="180" y="180" font-size="14" fill="#333333" font-weight="bold">C2</text>
  <!-- C3 -->
  <line x1="100" y1="140" x2="70" y2="125" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="45" y="125" font-size="14" fill="#800080" font-weight="bold">OH</text>
  <line x1="100" y1="140" x2="100" y2="175" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="96" y="190" font-size="14" fill="#000000">H</text>
  <text x="110" y="145" font-size="14" fill="#333333" font-weight="bold">C3</text>
  <!-- C4 -->
  <line x1="100" y1="80" x2="65" y2="80" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="40" y="85" font-size="14" fill="#800080" font-weight="bold">OH</text>
  <text x="105" y="75" font-size="14" fill="#000000">H</text>
  <text x="110" y="95" font-size="14" fill="#333333" font-weight="bold">C4</text>
  <!-- C5 -->
  <text x="155" y="45" font-size="14" fill="#333333" font-weight="bold">C5</text>
  <line x1="170" y1="50" x2="170" y2="20" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="145" y="15" font-size="14" fill="#000000">CH<tspan font-size="10" dy="3">2</tspan><tspan font-size="14" dy="-3">OH (C6)</tspan></text>
</svg>
</div>
<p>Which carbon atom corresponds to the anomeric carbon (the aldehyde carbon before cyclisation)?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1</strong><br/>Glucose forms a six-membered cyclic hemiacetal pyranose ring through the intramolecular nucleophilic addition of the hydroxyl group at C5 to the aldehyde carbonyl group at C1.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2</strong><br/>Before ring closure, C1 is an sp<sup>2</sup>-hybridized achiral carbonyl carbon. Upon cyclisation, C1 becomes an asymmetric stereocenter bearing both a ring oxygen and a hydroxyl group.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3</strong><br/>Isomers that differ specifically in the stereochemical configuration at this newly formed asymmetric hemiacetal carbon atom are termed anomers, and C1 is defined as the anomeric carbon.</p>
<p><strong>Final Answer</strong><br/>Carbon atom C1 is the anomeric carbon.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>C1</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>C2</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>C4</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>C5</p>]]></text></answer>
