  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_CHEMISTRY_BIOMOLECULES_DIAGRAM_Q03 - Identification of peptide linkage in dipeptides</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The synthesis of the dipeptide glycylalanine (Gly-Ala) is depicted in the following scheme:</p>
<div style="text-align:center; margin:10px 0;">
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 460 210" width="460" height="210" style="background:#ffffff; font-family:sans-serif;">
  <!-- Reactants -->
  <text x="15" y="45" font-size="15" fill="#000000">H<tspan font-size="11" dy="3">2</tspan><tspan font-size="15" dy="-3">N—CH</tspan><tspan font-size="11" dy="3">2</tspan><tspan font-size="15" dy="-3">—COOH</tspan></text>
  <text x="145" y="45" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#000000">+</text>
  <text x="175" y="45" font-size="15" fill="#000000">H<tspan font-size="11" dy="3">2</tspan><tspan font-size="15" dy="-3">N—CH(CH</tspan><tspan font-size="11" dy="3">3</tspan><tspan font-size="15" dy="-3">)—COOH</tspan></text>
  <text x="35" y="68" font-size="13" fill="#555555">(Glycine)</text>
  <text x="210" y="68" font-size="13" fill="#555555">(Alanine)</text>
  <!-- Downward arrow with -H2O -->
  <line x1="220" y1="80" x2="220" y2="125" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="2"/>
  <polygon points="220,125 215,115 225,115" fill="#000000"/>
  <text x="230" y="105" font-size="14" fill="#d9534f">− H<tspan font-size="10" dy="3">2</tspan><tspan font-size="14" dy="-3">O</tspan></text>
  <!-- Product -->
  <text x="30" y="165" font-size="16" fill="#000000">H<tspan font-size="12" dy="3">2</tspan><tspan font-size="16" dy="-3">N—CH</tspan><tspan font-size="12" dy="3">2</tspan><tspan font-size="16" dy="-3">—</tspan></text>
  <!-- Box around CO-NH -->
  <rect x="135" y="140" width="90" height="36" fill="#fff0f5" stroke="#c71585" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="142" y="165" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#c71585">CO—NH</text>
  <text x="230" y="165" font-size="16" fill="#000000">—CH(CH<tspan font-size="12" dy="3">3</tspan><tspan font-size="16" dy="-3">)—COOH</tspan></text>
  <!-- Pointer to X -->
  <line x1="180" y1="176" x2="180" y2="195" stroke="#c71585" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <text x="160" y="205" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#c71585">Linkage X</text>
</svg>
</div>
<p>What is the chemical name of the connecting functional unit labeled as "Linkage X"?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1</strong><br/>The reaction between two \(\alpha\)-amino acid molecules proceeds through condensation between the carboxyl group (\(-\mathrm{COOH}\)) of one molecule and the amino group (\(-\mathrm{NH_2}\)) of the other molecule.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2</strong><br/>This condensation results in the elimination of a water molecule and the formation of a covalent amide bond, represented by \(-\mathrm{CO-NH}-\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 3</strong><br/>In protein chemistry, this specific amide bond linking amino acid residues in peptides and proteins is termed a peptide bond or peptide linkage.</p>
<p><strong>Final Answer</strong><br/>Linkage X is chemically known as a peptide linkage (amide bond).</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Glycosidic linkage (ether bond)</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Phosphodiester linkage</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Peptide linkage (amide bond)</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Ester linkage</p>]]></text></answer>
