    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Structure (I) is \(\beta\)-D-2-deoxyribose, while Structure (II) is \(\beta\)-D-ribose, which is present in DNA</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Structure (I) is \(\beta\)-D-ribose, while Structure (II) is \(\beta\)-D-2-deoxyribose, which is present in DNA</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Structure (I) is \(\beta\)-D-ribose, while Structure (II) is \(\beta\)-D-2-deoxyribose, which is present in RNA</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Structure (I) is \(\alpha\)-D-glucopyranose, while Structure (II) is \(\beta\)-D-fructofuranose, which is present in RNA</p>]]></text></answer>
